,\n      \"com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver\",\n      \"jakarta\",\n      \"oracle.jdbc.driver.OracleDriver\",\n      \"org.h2.Driver\",\n      \"org.hibernate\",\n      \"org.hsqldb.jdbc.JDBCDriver\",\n      \"org.mariadb.jdbc.Driver\",\n      \"org.postgresql.Driver\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata-version\": \"6.1.1.Final\",\n    \"tested-versions\": [\n      \"6.1.1.Final\"\n    ],\n    \"source-code-url\": \"https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/hibernate/orm/hibernate-core/$version$/hibernate-core-$version$-sources.jar\",\n    \"repository-url\": \"https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm\",\n    \"test-code-url\": \"https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/tree/6.1.1/hibernate-core/src/test\",\n    \"documentation-url\": \"https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/hibernate/orm/hibernate-core/$version$/hibernate-core-$version$-javadoc.jar\",\n    \"description\": \"Hibernate ORM provides the core object-relational mapping functionality of Hibernate for mapping Java objects to relational database tables. It implements Jakarta Persistence (JPA) and also exposes Hibernate's native SessionFactory and Session APIs for querying, transactions, and entity lifecycle management.\"\n  }\n]\n\n--- trace config file inventory ---\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-0/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-1/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-2/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-3/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-4/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-5/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-6/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-7/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-8/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-9/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-10/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-11/reachability-metadata.json\ntests/src/org.hibernate/hibernate-core/6.1.0.Final/build/natively-collected/runs/cycle-12/reachability-metadata.json\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787942705860}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_lbCzA49UZiDr68Uxx1MckgxY|fc_015418e5c241b9f5016a91d731b68087d29434bb9cfaf4d6be", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "docs/functional-spec/metadata.md:1:# FS-metadata: The `metadata/` suite\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:1:# FS-test-contract: The test contract\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-28-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-29-> **Adding this repository to a user's build must never change how the user's code runs.** The metadata is purely additive — it can only fill in registrations `native-image` would otherwise miss; it cannot alter class initialization, replace user bytecode, or execute code at image-build time.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-30-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:31:Two properties make this achievable: the reachability-metadata schema is itself additive (every entry is gated on `typeReached`), and `native-image` defaults to runtime initialization when no build-time directives are supplied. The hard constraints below preserve that additivity — they are not editorial scope choices but direct consequences of the invariant.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-32-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-33-- **No build-time-initialization tweaks.** Metadata bundles must not ship `native-image.properties` or any other directive that moves class `<clinit>` execution into the image builder. Build-time initialization captures state from a non-user environment into the image and breaks additivity. Every library is runtime-initialized by default.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-34-- **No library patching.** No substitutions, bytecode rewrites, or shaded forks of upstream libraries. Patching ships a different version than the one the user resolved through Maven Central, is invisible at the dependency-resolution layer, and is unstable across upstream releases.\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-54-A Gradle-based TCK that, given a library coordinate `group:artifact:version`, runs:\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-55-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-56-- Validation of `index.json` schema and `metadata-version`/`tested-versions` integrity.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:57:- Validation that every metadata entry uses `typeReached` and stays inside `allowed-packages`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-58-- Compilation, JVM-mode tests (`javaTest`), and native-image tests (`nativeTest`).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-59-- Coverage collection (JaCoCo) and dynamic-access reporting per coordinate.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-60-\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-180-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-181-The schema follows semver. **Minor- and patch-version bumps** (e.g., `v2.1.0` → `v2.1.1` or `v2.1.x` → `v2.2.0`) are guaranteed backward-compatible with native-build-tools: minor bumps add new optional fields or non-plugin index formats used by the website, the test harness, or future tooling (`requires`, `test-version`, `skipped-versions`, `language`, `source-code-url`, `test-code-url`, `documentation-url`, `repository-url`, `not-for-native-image`, `auto-update`, `high-priority`); patch bumps refine validation of those same auxiliary fields and formats. The plugin reads only the six fields enumerated above, so an older native-build-tools release continues to resolve metadata correctly against any newer minor or patch version of the schema. A **major-version bump** (e.g., `v2.x` → `v3.0.0`) is reserved for changes that native-build-tools itself must adopt; it is shipped in lockstep with a plugin release rather than absorbed silently by older plugins.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-182-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:183:**3. `<groupId>/<artifactId>/<metadata-version>/reachability-metadata.json`** — the only file the plugin loads at native-image time. Schema [reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json](../../metadata/schemas/reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json) (a vendored copy of the upstream GraalVM schema), with top-level keys `reflection`, `jni`, `resources`, `bundles`, `serialization`, and `foreignCalls`. Every entry's `condition` carries exactly one key, `typeReached`, so the plugin can rely on conditional registration; `typeReached` is the schema's only condition form. The legacy split-config layout (`reflect-config.json`, `jni-config.json`, …) is no longer present.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-184-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-185-**4. Version-selection algorithm.** Given an application dependency `g:a:v`, native-build-tools loads the `index.json` array of `g/a/` and applies a primary lookup, picking the first entry that matches in this order:\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-186-\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-217-### 5.1 Metadata content\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-218-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-219-- **Metadata-only bundles.** Metadata files contain only JSON entries described by GraalVM's manual-configuration reference. Native-image properties (`native-image.properties`) and other build-time tweaks are forbidden — by default every library is runtime-initialized.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:220:- **Conditional registration.** Every metadata entry must use [Conditional Configuration](https://www.graalvm.org/latest/reference-manual/native-image/metadata/#specifying-reflection-metadata-in-json): a `condition` whose only key is `typeReached`, so registration is gated on actual reachability. `typeReached` is the sole condition form the vendored schema accepts; the older `typeReachable` is not valid and is rejected by `checkMetadataFiles`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:221:- **Allowed-package conditions.** Every metadata entry's `typeReached` condition must reference a class inside the artifact's `allowed-packages`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-222-- **No test-only shipped entries.** A metadata entry is test-only when the type it describes belongs to a package from the test suite; such entries must not ship. A type from the library JAR or one of its dependencies is library metadata even when a test is what exercised it.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-223-- **Index coverage.** Each `metadata/<group>/<artifact>/` directory must include a valid `index.json` enumerating its metadata versions and tested library versions.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-224-- **Single latest entry.** Exactly one entry in a non-empty `index.json` must carry `latest: true`. If a library version is not in `tested-versions`, the harness selects an entry by matching the optional `default-for` regex.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:225:- **Dependency and test-only split.** Metadata can declare dependencies on other artifacts via `requires`. Metadata needed only by the tests — entries whose type or `typeReached` names a test package, or whose resource is a test resource — must not ship to consumers; `splitTestOnlyMetadata` moves them out of the library's `reachability-metadata.json` into the test project's `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json`, keeping the shipped metadata free of test-only types (§FS-metadata).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-226-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-227-### 5.2 Tests\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-228-\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-272-\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-273-- **Determinism.** Tests must be reproducible. Network-dependent tests are not allowed except where they declare an `allowed-docker-image` and run against that pre-pulled image with networking disabled.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-274-- **Isolation.** Per-coordinate test execution must not depend on or affect other coordinates' build outputs.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:275:- **Image-size discipline.** Conditional configuration (`typeReached`) is mandatory so consumers do not pay for metadata they do not exercise.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-276-- **Schema fidelity.** Every JSON file under `metadata/`, `stats/`, and `metadata/library-and-framework-list.json` must validate against the corresponding schema in `schemas/` or `stats/schemas/` (§PRCPL-verify-inputs).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-277-- **Style consistency.** All Java/Groovy/Gradle/shell sources must pass `spotlessCheck` (CC0 license header) and `checkstyle`. JSON is sorted by keys, indented with two spaces.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-278-- **Sharded scalability.** Any Gradle task that accepts `-Pcoordinates=` must accept `k/n` shards so CI can parallelize. The harness must handle adding a new library without code changes (purely metadata-driven discovery).\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-385-§forge/AR-forge-orchestration); the bulk-update PR is reviewed by the\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-386-`review-library-bulk-update` skill. This section is the behavioral contract for\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-387-that workflow; the run-size limits are stated in §FS-repository-functional-spec.5.3\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:388:and the recording precondition in §FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2, and every\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-389-label it applies is defined in the\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-390-§4.6 GitHub label contract.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md-391-\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-52-\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-53-## 2. Invariants\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-54-\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:55:- **Conditional on `typeReached`, and nothing else.** Every reachability-metadata\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:56:  entry is gated on a `condition` whose only key is `typeReached`.\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:57:  `typeReached` is the sole condition key the vendored schema accepts; no other\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:58:  condition form — including the older `typeReachable` — is valid, and\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-59-  `checkMetadataFiles` rejects any entry that uses one. The reached type must lie\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-60-  inside the artifact's `allowed-packages`, and no entry may target a test-only\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-61-  type (§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1). No build-time-initialization\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-80-test classes, fixtures, and resources that exercise the library — but those\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-81-entries must never reach a consumer (§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1). The\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-82-harness `splitTestOnlyMetadata` task (§AR-test-harness.5) maintains that\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:83:separation: any entry whose `type` or `condition.typeReached` names a test\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-84-package, or whose resource is a test resource, is moved out of the library's\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md-85-`metadata/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/reachability-metadata.json` and into the\ndocs/funct